# Project-basic residual risk report

## Residual risks after scoped verification

| Risk | Status | Residual impact | Owner decision needed? |
|---|---|---|---|
| Guidance may not feel more useful than ordinary chat for the intended beginner and creative audiences. | Open qualitative risk | Moderate | Yes. Observe the documented dogfood scenarios before treating the experience as proven. |
| The lack of dedicated CLI guidance commands may reduce discoverability of rich pack guidance. | Accepted scope limitation | Low to moderate | No decision within this successor; consider a later successor only if observed friction warrants it. |
| No full local pytest-suite final summary is recorded. | Open validation limitation | Moderate | Yes for any broader release decision; re-run the full suite in a terminal or CI that produces durable results. |
| Historical Local Production-v1 candidate bytes cannot validate changed source. | Controlled and documented | Low | No. The version-consistency report labels that candidate historical only; a future candidate requires separate authority. |
| Project-specific checks validate structure and exact support, not semantic quality of a future created-work artifact. | Inherent governance boundary | Moderate | Yes for each real project: owner review and acceptance remain required. |
| A user may misread conversational authorization envelopes as persisted approval. | Mitigated presentation risk | Low | No immediate decision. Guidance/docs repeatedly state envelopes are bounded, revocable, and presentation-only. |
| A user may mistake a branch push or later CI result for FORGE closure or release approval. | Mitigated coordination risk | Low | No immediate decision. The Git/closure guide requires separately authorized acceptance and terminal closure, and records CI as independently reviewable evidence. |

## Release boundary

This review does not recommend, authorize, or imply a release, tag, publication, framework version
bump, or replacement production candidate. It supports only the scoped conclusion that the
experimental pack is structurally implemented and validated within the limitations in the accepted
verification report.

## Suggested owner observation

Use the dogfood guide with beginner game, scientific/evidence, physical-making, creative-writing or
song, and clear-software scenarios. Preserve exact revisions and owner-observed facts. Record
whether vision capture, context, questions, teaching, delegation, confusion reduction, and the
experience relative to ordinary chat justify any future expansion.
